 "fields": [
  {
   "field": "Document",
   "value": "TBCA Deliverables Resources File — control register of every customer deliverable on the TBCA WebApp and Platform, now covering all 7,589 Sprints"
  },
  {
   "field": "Issue",
   "value": "MP-DEL-2.0 · Issue 2.0 · 23 October 2026 (supersedes MP-DEL-1.0 of the same date; nothing in Issue 1.0 has been removed or shortened)"
  },
  {
   "field": "Prepared by",
   "value": "Claude Opus 5.5 (Max) for The Business Clinic.Africa"
  },
  {
   "field": "Instrument",
   "value": "Executes Master Prompt MP-DEL-2.0 and prompts D0–D20 (companion Word booklet)"
  },
  {
   "field": "Coverage",
   "value": "8,318 deliverables = 861 Issue-1.0 deliverables (all retained) + 7,457 new deliverables from the Sprint catalogue. 132 Sprints matched an Issue-1.0 deliverable and were linked to it, not duplicated. All 7,589 Sprints are accounted for in the Sprint Crosswalk sheet."
  },
  {
   "field": "Sources added in Issue 2.0",
   "value": "TBCA_Batch_4A/4B/4C/4D Sprint Workbooks REPRICED_v3 (7,589 Sprints); 04_R0C_ECON-R0C-CATALOGUE-7589 (prices and viability); TBCA Implementation Bible MP-BIBLE-1.1 FINAL (AAI NOW: OSS-17 stages, loops, safeguards, platforms); HeyGen and Infogram product documentation"
  },
  {
   "field": "Format rule",
   "value": "Columns A–W keep the Issue-1.0 format exactly. Columns X–AW (gold headers) are the Issue-2.0 additions required by the brief: catalogue package content, the V2 depth uplift, the wow layer, AI depth, HeyGen and Infogram layers, automation route, payment-triggered loop, acceptance parameters and safeguards."
  },
  {
   "field": "Standards",
   "value": "The Standards sheet carries the Issue-1.0 parameters. The client's yellow-highlighted revision had not been received in readable form at issue (the uploaded copy was identical to Issue 1.0); every page and SLA figure is held as a parameter and re-applies automatically when the revision is supplied."
  },
  {
   "field": "Status",
   "value": "Design control — PROPOSED standards for TBCA approval. Prices are quoted from the catalogue only; this file does not set prices."
  },
  {
   "field": "Owner",
   "value": "TBCA Head of Delivery & QA; automation owner BP-29 Sprint Automation Authority"
  },
  {
   "field": "Tier mapping",
   "value": "Basic = Clinic Starter; Standard = Growth Sprint; Premium = Board Ready Sprint."
  },
  {
   "field": "Depth = v1 extent + V2 uplift",
   "value": "For every deliverable the tier content is the Issue-1.0 extent (columns I–K) PLUS the V2 depth uplift (columns AL–AN), the HeyGen and Infogram layers and the beyond-benchmark value. Nothing is removed."
  },
  {
   "field": "Automation",
   "value": "Delivery follows the AAI NOW Implementation Bible: OSS-17 stages, bounded loops, L3 SUPERVISED at NOW (a qualified person releases every order), promotion to L4 only on BP-29 evidence."
  },
  {
   "field": "Trigger",
   "value": "EVT-006 Payment Confirmed (signed PayFast webhook, amount = invoice) starts the Sprint's delivery loop automatically. The delivery clock starts at intake completion (OSS-S8), not at payment."
  },
  {
   "field": "Sources",
   "value": "Live WebApp · Blueprint · AIIM Botswana · Prototype · Proposed · Sprint catalogue (Batch 4A–4D) — every row says which."
  },
  {
   "field": "Professional boundary",
   "value": "Regulated opinions are routed to registered partners (SG-12). AI never approves a regulated decision."
  }
 ],
